{"term":"lookout","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a76ae1e895437df454","definition":"A vantage point with a view of the surrounding area.","example":"Gulangyu island has a spectacular crows-nest lookout reached by winding stone staircases. From so high, the Nationalist islands look like lumps of cookie batter dropped onto the smooth harbor, with picturesque sailing junks not far away.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sentry","surveillance","vigil","watch"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on the lookout","be-on-the-lookout","fire lookout tower","keep a lookout","lookout man","lookout tower","on the lookout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lookout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6fbce84d2a4fedd4d5","definition":"A session of watching for an approaching enemy, police, etc.","example":"We kept a lookout all night, but nobody came.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sentry","surveillance","vigil","watch"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on the lookout","be-on-the-lookout","fire lookout tower","keep a lookout","lookout man","lookout tower","on the lookout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lookout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0673abe520de61b6f8","definition":"A person on watch for approaching enemy, police, danger, etc.","example":"The raid failed when the lookout noticed the enemy group.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["lookout man","watchout"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on the lookout","be-on-the-lookout","fire lookout tower","keep a lookout","lookout man","lookout tower","on the lookout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lookout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1dac3a66ba274d62ea","definition":"A subject for observation; a prospect or view.","example":"Looking, seeing: search or searching; Looking-for (B.), expectation; Lookout, a careful watching for: an elevated place from which to observe: one engaged in watching. And, you know, she OUGHT to keep enough to pay for her season-ticket; but no, she comes to me about that, and I have to find the money.\"\n\"It's a poor lookout,\" said Mrs. Morel bitterly.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sentry","surveillance","vigil","watch"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on the lookout","be-on-the-lookout","fire lookout tower","keep a lookout","lookout man","lookout tower","on the lookout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lookout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f7a489708dbf38f5b9","definition":"One's perspective, outlook; hence, one's responsibility. (used with a possessive pronoun or a noun in a possessive form).","example":"Every person's interest is his own lookout.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sentry","surveillance","vigil","watch"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on the lookout","be-on-the-lookout","fire lookout tower","keep a lookout","lookout man","lookout tower","on the lookout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lookout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e5fe89d123af1916f8","definition":"An observation window.","example":"Twenty-one of these vehicles were later converted into bogie brake vans for freight service. [...] The extreme width over the side lookouts is 9 ft.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["sentry","surveillance","vigil","watch"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["be on t